{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Penpot Design Sync Validator",
  "description": "After editing a component file, validates visual properties against Penpot source of truth. Checks badge colors, button alignment, theme tokens, component specs, and layout positioning.",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "apps/*/src/components/*.tsx",
      "apps/*/src/screens/*.tsx"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A component or screen file was just edited. Read the file and validate against Penpot specs (from .kiro/steering/penpot-to-code-app.md):\n\nCRITICAL CHECKS:\n1. Badge text color: Status badges use TINTED style — background is statusColor@12% opacity, text is the statusColor itself. NEVER '#FFFFFF' for status badges.\n2. Badge fontWeight: ALWAYS '400' for ALL sizes. NEVER '500' or '600'.\n3. Button alignSelf: MUST be 'center' (centered in card). NEVER 'flex-start'.\n4. Button sm fontWeight: MUST be '400'. NEVER '500'.\n5. Button color for aguardando: MUST use primary (#7B2D2D), NOT the status color.\n6. Card gradient: Status cards MUST have LinearGradient overlay (transparent→10% status color).\n7. Card stroke opacity: MUST use 30% (hex suffix '4D').\n8. Origin display: MUST use tinted badge (View with bg + styled Text), NOT plain Text component.\n9. Price text: MUST be fontSize 18, fontWeight '600'.\n10. RN ROTATION POSITIONING: Penpot coordinates do NOT translate 1:1 to React Native for rotated elements. RN rotates around the element center AFTER layout, so positions must be empirically adjusted. For the PrototypeBanner ribbon (111×18, rotate 45°, clip box 80×80 positioned at top:56 right:0 — below AppBar): the correct RN values are clip top: 56, ribbon top: 23, left: -8 (NOT the raw Penpot coords). NEVER change these values based on Penpot coordinate math alone.\n11. Payment screen layout: The '+ Adicionar Item' button MUST be positioned directly below the items list (inside the 'Itens do pedido' section with marginTop: 12), NEVER after the 'Confirmar Pagamento' button.\n12. Calendar day cells: Day cells in calendar grids MUST use justifyContent: 'start' (top-aligned), NEVER 'center'. This ensures numbers align at the top regardless of whether an indicator dot is present.\n13. Payment method selected state: Selected method uses solid bg #5A8C5A (success green) + text #FFFFFF. Unselected uses bg #FFFFFF + border #E8DDD5 + text #3D2020.\n14. Switch Toggle: trackColor active=#7B2D2D, inactive=#E8DDD5. Thumb always #FFFFFF.\n15. Drawer Menu: Logout lives ONLY in the drawer. No logout icon in AppBar.\n\nIf ANY deviations found, fix them immediately. Reference .kiro/steering/penpot-to-code-app.md for the full spec."
  },
  "workspaceFolderName": "order-system",
  "shortName": "penpot-design-sync"
}